Scene II: മഹാമനുഷ്യൻ നിർമ്മിക്കുന്നു.

[Enter Falstaff and Rosalind]
Rosalind:
 You are a hero.
Falstaff:
 You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.

Scene III: കൃത്യമായ ഇരട്ടിക്കൽ.

Falstaff:
 Are you better than nothing?
Rosalind:
 If not, let us proceed to scene IV.
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.
Falstaff:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 Let us return to scene III.

Scene IV: മഹാമനുഷ്യന്റെ അവസാന കുറവ്.

Rosalind:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene V: seed മൂല്യം നിർമ്മിച്ച് SAVE ചെയ്യുന്നു.

[Enter Falstaff and Beatrice]
Falstaff:
 You are as good as the product of Ophelia and Juliet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of Cordelia and Romeo.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of Desdemona and Othello.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of Portia and Macbeth.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of Viola and Lady Macbeth.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big hero and a hero and Miranda.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big big hero and a hero and Ariel.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Falstaff.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
